# Xcode
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Left behind by a local `xcodebuild test`, and by the CI workflow.
build.log
*.xcresult

# Screenshots taken by CI, which writes into Quiet/shots.
#
# Anchored. Unanchored, `shots/` matches at every depth — and the depth it also
# matched was Tools/shots, which is not CI's output at all: it is the source
# photographs the listing is built from. They were not in the repository, and
# nobody could tell, because a file that was never added does not show up as
# missing.
/shots/

# The finished slides, which `Tools/make-shots.py` writes and can write again.
#
# The frames they are cut from are kept — `Tools/shots/originals` and
# `Tools/shots/source` are tracked on purpose, because a slide that cannot be
# re-cut from its own frame has to be re-shot from scratch. The slides
# themselves are output: thirty-three megabytes of it, in every clone, for
# something one command reproduces.
Tools/shots/out/

# Left by running anything in Tools/.
__pycache__/

# Written by Tools/look-at-icon.py, for looking at rather than keeping.
Tools/icon-in-place.png
